From 0d2d7df76746a11458424a927edb64c8ea18c425 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: banil246 <igoigo246@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:28:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] koedodb: per-Worker resource limits for the open-source
 server

The open-source workerd server uses NullIsolateLimitEnforcer / NullLimitEnforcer ('Single-tenant policy:
no limits'), so one Worker can stop all the others in the process. This adds real enforcers for Workers that
have limits, in a new file (src/workerd/server/factory/koedodb-limits.{h,c++}); Workers without limits keep the
original Null enforcers.

Limits per Worker (0 = none): cpuMs (thread CPU time of a request, summed over its JS runs), wallMs (wall
clock of a request), heapMb (V8 old generation of the Worker's isolate), externalMb (ArrayBuffer / typed
array / WebAssembly memory, through a counting ArrayBuffer::Allocator), subrequests (per request).
CPU and wall time are watched by one watchdog thread that calls TerminateExecution() on that isolate only;
the heap limit uses ResourceConstraints plus a near-heap-limit callback that ends the running request and
gives the heap room to unwind (a refusal of the ArrayBuffer allocator that V8 reports through the same
callback while the heap is far from full is not treated as heap exhaustion: the tenant gets its RangeError).
After a termination the isolate is resumed (CancelTerminateExecution) so the Worker's next request works.
Exceeded limits are reported through the existing LimitEnforcer hooks (onLimitsExceeded, getLimitsExceeded,
requireLimitsNotExceeded) with the CPU / WALL_TIME / MEMORY detail IDs.

The limits come from WORKERD_KOEDODB_LIMITS (or the file named by WORKERD_KOEDODB_LIMITS_FILE):
  <worker name>|*=cpu:50,wall:5000,heap:64,ext:128,sub:50 ; ...

Edits outside the new file: three small ones in worker-factory.c++ (create the isolate enforcer and the request
enforcer through the new functions; the isolate group is made before the enforcer so that the counting
allocator can wrap the group's default allocator) and the two names in the factory's BUILD.bazel.
